# Everything here is excluded from the build *context* — the tarball sent to
# the daemon before the first instruction runs. Two reasons to care.
#
# Speed: `.venv/` alone is hundreds of megabytes, and it is uploaded on every
# build whether or not a COPY ever mentions it.
#
# Correctness: a stray `.env` or `.venv` in the context is one careless
# `COPY . .` away from being in the image. Excluding it here means the mistake
# cannot be made, rather than being one somebody has to remember not to make.

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# A virtualenv built for the host, useless in the image and enormous.
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets. Nothing in this repository copies them, and that is exactly the kind
# of guarantee that quietly stops being true.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Not needed to build or run the application. Tests deliberately do not ship:
# an image that contains its own test suite is one somebody will eventually run
# tests in, against production configuration.
tests/
docs/
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
